[{"id":3006775044,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6zN78E","user":{"login":"anvilfolk","id":1133892,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzM4OTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1133892?u=f7b9e7e46e23ecc739f717e262e406f139e7a3c1&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anvilfolk","html_url":"https://github.com/anvilfolk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anvilfolk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anvilfolk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anvilfolk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anvilfolk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anvilfolk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anvilfolk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anvilfolk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anvilfolk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anvilfolk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR looks a little cleaner, but I'm worried it is a little less robust than https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107699.\r\n\r\nDoc regen/load (for native and script classes) happens in a couple of different awkward places (I believe somewhere in GDExtension-world too), so having the checks inside `EditorHelp` makes it a bit more fool-proof, IMO.\r\n \r\nThis PR is using `EditorNode::cmdline_mode`, which is set on `export_preset()` or if there's no available `DisplayServer`, as opposed to `main.cpp::cmdline_tool` from the other PR, which is set for specific command-line options.\r\n\r\nBoth approaches leave me worried that they might stop docload/docgen when it is desired. For example, wouldn't we want docs loaded with `--doctool`? That sets `main.cpp::cmdline_tool = true`, and I'm guessing it would make `cmdline_mode = true` as well.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107685#pullreque